✅ try...catch kya hota hai?
try...catch ek error-handling structure hai. Iska use hum runtime errors ko handle karne ke liye karte hain — taki program crash na ho.

🔹 Syntax:
javascript

try {
  // Code jo error throw kar sakta hai
} catch (error) {
  // Error aane par yahaan handle karte hain
}
🔹 Example:
javascript

try {
  let a = x + 1;  // 'x' is not defined → Error
} catch (err) {
  console.log("Error aaya:", err.message);
}
🟢 Output:

vbnet

Error aaya: x is not defined
🔹 With finally (optional):
javascript

try {
  // risky code
} catch (err) {
  // handle error
} finally {
  // yeh block hamesha chalega, chahe error aaye ya nahi
}
✅ Use Cases:
API calls mein error handle karna

File read/write operations

User input validation

Asynchronous code (async/await) ke saath

🔹 Real-world async example:
javascript

async function fetchData() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");
    const data = await res.json();
    console.log(data);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("API error:", error.message);
  }
}
